Astro is an excellent choice for EULOK's company website. For a software development company website that is primarily content, services, case studies, documentation and lead generation, I would choose Astro over Next.js.

The key distinction: FAANG-grade describes the quality of the engineering, design, security and operations—not the framework or the complexity of the architecture.

Astro's static-first architecture is particularly appropriate for a company site serving visitors in Uganda and internationally. You can deliver pre-rendered pages with very little client-side JavaScript, then add interactive functionality only where it provides value.

I would revise several parts of the blueprint you shared:

- Do not choose Next.js merely because large technology companies use React.
- Do not introduce microservices, Redis or a database unless actual requirements justify them.
- Do not promise 99.99% availability without the infrastructure, budget and operational capability to support it.
- Do not treat Lighthouse scores as a substitute for real-user performance monitoring.
- Do not assume Cloudflare automatically makes every page fast in Uganda. Measure performance from actual Ugandan networks and devices.

