Your website must remain useful under slower and less consistent network conditions.

I would enforce these requirements:

- Mobile-first layout, not desktop design compressed onto mobile.
- Optimize for common Android devices and modest hardware.
- Minimize JavaScript execution and download size.
- Avoid large autoplay videos.
- Avoid large background images.
- Use AVIF/WebP where suitable.
- Specify image dimensions to prevent layout shifts.
- Use responsive image sizes.
- Prefer local or reliably cached fonts.
- Avoid excessive external scripts.
- Make the important content available before nonessential animations load.
- Ensure navigation and contact mechanisms work without JavaScript wherever practical.

A particularly important detail: a global CDN does not prove that every Ugandan ISP will deliver the site quickly. Actual routing, peering, congestion and device capability matter.

Test from real Ugandan connections rather than relying exclusively on a Lighthouse test performed on your development computer.

