# 9. CI/CD and production quality gates

This is where the site stops being merely a website and becomes a properly engineered product.

I would use GitHub Actions as the independent quality authority.

Every pull request should run the following pipeline:

## Production release pipeline

1. Code quality

   Formatting, linting, TypeScript checks and Astro diagnostics.
2. Automated tests

   Unit tests, component tests and integration tests.
3. Security

   Dependency scanning, secret detection and configuration checks.
4. Build verification

   Production build, broken-link checks, metadata checks and asset budgets.
5. Browser testing

   Playwright functional, responsive and regression testing.
6. Accessibility

   Automated axe scans and relevant accessibility checks.
7. Performance

   Lighthouse CI, JavaScript budgets and image budgets.
8. Preview deployment

   Review the actual production build before release.
9. Production deployment

   Deploy only after required quality gates pass.
10. Post-deployment verification

    Check critical routes, headers, forms, redirects and production health.

